   "claims": [
    "Cubic Yards Volume Formulas Frequently Asked Questions By Joe Sexton Joe is the creator of Inch Calculator and has over 20 years of experience in engineering and construction.",
    "cu yd = Lft × Wft × Hft / 27 The steps to find cubic yards using this method are: Measure the width, length, and height of the space in feet.",
    "Finally, convert the cubic feet measurement to cubic yards by dividing the result by 27, since cubic yards are equal to cubic feet ÷ 27.",
    "For example, let’s calculate the cubic yards for a space that is 12 ft long by 14 ft wide by 9 inches deep.",
    "depth = 9 inches ÷ 12 depth = 0.75 feet Next, calculate the volume in cubic feet.",
    "cu ft = 12 ft × 14 ft × 0.75 ft cu ft = 126 cu ft Finally, convert the volume in cubic feet to cubic yards.",
    "cu yds = 126 cu ft ÷ 27 cu yds = 4.67 cu yds If you are calculating yardage for a concrete or landscaping project, understand that suppliers may not sell fractions of a yard of material.",
    "yds3 = length × width × height Round or Cylinder Formula Calculate the volume in cubic yards of a cylinder using the formula πr2h, where r is the radius of the cylinder’s base and h is its height.",
    "There are 27 cubic feet in a cubic yard.",
    "This is variable depending on what kind of truck, but the volume of a 2022 Toyota Tacoma 6-foot truck bed is only 1.252 cubic yards."
   ],
